%I A092647 #20 Sep 05 2026 23:45:40
%S A092647 0,0,1,5,13,34,207,349,631,1257,2295,19785,47882
%N A092647 Absolute value of difference between counts of uninterrupted runs of 4 primes in A092645 and A092646.
%C A092647 Take the absolute value of the difference between counts of runs of 4 primes congruent to 1 mod 4 and 3 mod 4.
%H A092647 Carlo Corti, <a href="https://doi.org/10.5281/zenodo.22194072">A092645-A092647: maximal four-prime runs modulo 4</a>, Zenodo, 2026.
%F A092647 a(n) = abs(A092646(n) - A092645(n)). - _Michel Marcus_, Jun 03 2014
%e A092647 a(4)=5 because in A092645 the count is 10 and in A092646 the count is 15. 15 - 10 = 5.
%Y A092647 Cf. A092645, A092646.
%K A092647 more,nonn,changed
%O A092647 1,4
%A A092647 _Enoch Haga_, Mar 02 2004
%E A092647 a(9)-a(10), using A092645 and A092646, from _Michel Marcus_, Jun 03 2014
%E A092647 a(11) from _Chai Wah Wu_, Mar 18 2018
%E A092647 a(12)-a(13), using A092645 and A092646, from _Carlo Corti_, Aug 31 2026
